      "message": "Calling `trng_init()` and `trng_exit()` doesn\u0027t make sense in Zephyr FW, because these are [basically no-op](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/trng.h;l\u003d17-23;drc\u003d6757ebe2dce2a23e2cd3149eb82b32faa4f16908). It means that `test_trng_rand_bytes` and `test_trng_rand_bytes_toogle` are effectively the same tests, so we can remove the latter.\n\nAlso we should add Zephyr entropy tests to our test suite https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/tests/drivers/entropy/api/src/main.c. Zephyr entropy tests are not exactly the same as our tests, so we should keep both.",
